26	/**
27	 Safelists define what HTML (elements and attributes) to allow through a {@link Cleaner}. Everything else is removed.
28	 <p>
29	 Start with one of the defaults:
30	 </p>
31	 <ul>
32	 <li>{@link #none}
33	 <li>{@link #simpleText}
34	 <li>{@link #basic}
35	 <li>{@link #basicWithImages}
36	 <li>{@link #relaxed}
37	 </ul>
38	 <p>
39	 If you need to allow more through (please be careful!), tweak a base safelist with:
40	 </p>
41	 <ul>
42	 <li>{@link #addTags(String... tagNames)}
43	 <li>{@link #addAttributes(String tagName, String... attributes)}
44	 <li>{@link #addEnforcedAttribute(String tagName, String attribute, String value)}
45	 <li>{@link #addProtocols(String tagName, String attribute, String... protocols)}
46	 </ul>
47	 <p>
48	 You can remove any setting from an existing safelist with:
49	 </p>
50	 <ul>
51	 <li>{@link #removeTags(String... tagNames)}
52	 <li>{@link #removeAttributes(String tagName, String... attributes)}
53	 <li>{@link #removeEnforcedAttribute(String tagName, String attribute)}
54	 <li>{@link #removeProtocols(String tagName, String attribute, String... removeProtocols)}
55	 </ul>
56	
57	 <p>
58	 The {@link Cleaner} and these safelists assume that you want to clean a <code>body</code> fragment of HTML (to add user
59	 supplied HTML into a templated page), and not to clean a full HTML document. If the latter is the case, you could wrap
60	 the templated document HTML around the cleaned body HTML.
61	 </p>
62	 <p>
63	 Safelists are mutable. A {@link Cleaner} uses the supplied safelist directly, so later changes affect later cleaning
64	 calls. If you want to share a safelist across threads, finish configuring it first and do not mutate it while it is in
65	 use. To build a variant from an existing configuration, use {@link #Safelist(Safelist)} to make a copy.
66	 </p>
67	 <p>
68	 If you are going to extend a safelist, please be very careful. Make sure you understand what attributes may lead to
69	 XSS attack vectors. URL attributes are particularly vulnerable and require careful validation. See 
70	 the <a href="https://owasp.org/www-community/xss-filter-evasion-cheatsheet">XSS Filter Evasion Cheat Sheet</a> for some
71	 XSS attack examples (that jsoup will safeguard against with the default Cleaner and Safelist configuration).
72	 </p>
